1. Ke1 (1. c6 $143 g2 2. Ke1 g3 $19) g2 ({main} Kb7 $144 2. Kf1 Kc6 3. c4 $1 f2 4. Kg2 $1 ({Thematic try:} 4. Ke2 $143 g2 $1 5. Kxf2 f3 6. Kg1 g3 $11 {ZZ with White to play}) f3+ 5. Kf1 {Leads to a similar maneuver as in the main line or} g2+ 6. Kxf2 g3+ 7. Kg1 $18 {ZZ with black to play}) 2. Kf2 g3+ 3. Kg1 Kb7 4. c3 $1 ({Thematic try:} 4. c4 $143 Kc6 $1 5. Ba7 Kb7 6. Bb6 Kc6 $11 {ZZ with white to play}) Kc6 5. c4 $1 {ZZ with black to play} Kd7 6. Ba5 Kc6 7. Bb4 Kd7 8. Bc3 Kc6 9. Bd4 Kd7 10. Be5 $1 ({Thematic try:} 10. Bg7 $143 $1 Kc6 $1 11. Bf8 Kc7 {Or Kb7/Kd7} 12. Bd6+ Kc6 $11 {ZZ and the white Bishop , unable to make further progress is forced to retreat all the way back to d4 and to try again}) Kc6 11. Bd6 {ZZ with Black to play} Kd7 12. Bxf4 Kc6 13. Bd6 Kb7 14. Bxg3 Kc6 15. Bf2 $18 {and the Bishop finally concludes a 10 moves journey of consecutive zugzwangs enabling its King to finish off the battle. ------------ Surprisingly incredible maneuvers a white Bishop! The author has realized a modern study on high technical level!} 1-0

